        "id": 8825,
        "name": "Hummingbird",
        "username": "Hummingbird",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/59ef9b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-10-11T22:39:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm playing my first solo game that I plan to finish now and I discarded all the cards in hand (hypothetical other player) from one hero to destroy the Toxic Seaweed environment card. Now this hero doesn't have a hand of cards. Then the next villain card that was played was Baron Blade's \"Consider The Price of Victory makes each player discard 1 card...but one of my heroes (the one that destroyed Toxic Seaweed) doesn't have a hand of cards.</p><p>what happens next? Does that hero immediately draw 4 cards after discarding hand? Or does she (The Wraith) continue to play the game without a regular hand; depending entirely on drawing cards from the draw phase and abilties that allow card drawing?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thanks!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:39:27.062Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
