      {
        "id": 76907,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-10-11T22:48:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>If you have no cards in-hand and something tells you to discard, then you can't discard. So if \"Consider the Price of Victory!\" comes out there's a player with no cards, that's one less card that's going to be discarded. The only way to draw new cards is during your Draw phase (note - this is optional, as you never <span class=\"bbcode-i\">have</span> to play/power/draw during those phases of your turn) or if some other effect says you can. At no point do you ever automatically draw a card for no reason. There is also no maximum hand - you could have your entire deck in-hand if the game went on long enough and you never played or discarded anything. I've certainly played at least one game (possibly two, both as the Adept) where I had my entire deck out (not all cards were in-hand, though - some were in play).</p>\n<p>Note also that if something tells you you can \"discard your hand\" to do something (like Toxic Seaweed), a hand of zero cards is still a hand, so you can still \"discard\" it :).</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:57:42.761Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 8825,
        "topic_slug": "what-to-do-after-discarding-your-hand-of-cards",
        "display_username": "Ameena",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "If you have no cards in-hand and something tells you to discard, then you can&#39;t discard. So if &quot;Consider the Price of Victory!&quot; comes out there&#39;s a player with no cards, that&#39;s one less card that&#39;s going to be discarded. The only way to draw new cards is during your Draw phase (note - this is optional, as you never [i]have[/i] to play/power/draw during those phases of your turn) or if some other effect says you can. At no point do you ever automatically draw a card for no reason. There is also no maximum hand - you could have your entire deck in-hand if the game went on long enough and you never played or discarded anything. I&#39;ve certainly played at least one game (possibly two, both as the Adept) where I had my entire deck out (not all cards were in-hand, though - some were in play).\n\nNote also that if something tells you you can &quot;discard your hand&quot; to do something (like Toxic Seaweed), a hand of zero cards is still a hand, so you can still &quot;discard&quot; it :).\n",
