      {
        "id": 76908,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-10-12T05:23:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Note also that if something tells you you can \"discard your hand\" to do something (like Toxic Seaweed), a hand of zero cards is still a hand, so you can still \"discard\" it :).</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It has, however, been ruled that an Incapacitated hero no longer has a hand at all, and thus they cannot discard their hand.&nbsp; They <em>can</em> skip their turn, though…their turn normally consists of using one of their incap abilities, but they can give that up to delay a Self-Destruct Sequence or the like.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:57:42.862Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
